  "package_integrity": {
    "test": "codex_plugin_compat_t14_preserves_isolation / codex_plugin_compat_t14_retains_valid_siblings_and_normalized_aliases",
    "basis": "Real MCP file bytes are compared before/after discovery, merging and declaration normalization; commands and network services are not started. No installation or package rewriting occurs in declaration loading."
  },
  "observed_side_effects": [
    "Actual discovery/merge accepts wrapped maps, direct maps, existing arrays and inline objects. Legacy absent declarations use audited .mcp.json; explicit file/inline declarations override it across Codex/Claude/Cursor manifests.",
    "Named declaration keys remain routing identity; legacy display name is discarded. Transport follows command/url, not type, and OAuth camelCase aliases normalize with snake_case taking precedence. Empty environment values and argument bytes are preserved.",
    "File declaration outcomes retain valid siblings and per-server diagnostics. Runtime retains the existing strict failure contract: any invalid or unsupported server rejects the whole configuration before returning or mutating the caller with that configuration.",
    "Disabled packages and named disabled servers do not contribute runtime entries. User-defined names retain priority. Implicit default symlinks, including dangling links, fail existing path audit without reading the outside payload."
  ],
  "intentional_safety_differences": [
    "Reference parsing retains valid siblings and its runtime logs/skips invalid siblings. The host retains its existing stricter whole-config runtime rejection while exposing the normalized valid siblings and named diagnostics to the declaration loader.",
    "The host rejects non-string transport labels and malformed transport fields explicitly. No arbitrary unsupported runtime setting is silently dropped.",
    "Working directory/env references, OAuth/HTTP header policy, tool policy and lifecycle settings remain explicit runtime errors until owning tasks 16-23/26-28 implement them. Their normalized declarations are retained without a false execution claim."
  ],
